<title>BELGIUM: EU farm ministers to discuss reform plan on Tues.</title>
<headline>EU farm ministers to discuss reform plan on Tues.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers will hold a preliminary discussion on Tuesday of proposed agricultural reforms to prepare for EU expansion eastwards, a spokesman for the Luxembourg EU Presidency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The spokesman said ministers would exchange views over dinner after a formal presentation by EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler at a monthly EU farm council.</p>
<p>The reforms will be the focus of discussions during a three-day informal gathering of EU farm ministers in Echternach, Luxembourg, from September 7-9.</p>
<p>Luxembourg took over the rotating six-month EU Presidency from the Netherlands on July 1.</p>
<p>-Brussels bureau +322 287 6830</p>
